[For "white"]
[Kind "main"]
[Start "london-main 4.Nf3"]
[Name "Bishops: ...Bd6 at once"]

4... Bd6 { Offers the trade before anything else, to challenge the bishop that started the opening. }
5. Bg3 { The same reply as ever: step back along the diagonal and let Black decide. Black gets nothing from taking, and the h-file opens if it does. [%cal Gg3d6] }
5... O-O
6. Bd3 { Puts the bishop on its best square and prepares to castle. [%cal Gd3h7] }
6... c5
7. c3 { Backs up d4, as in the main line. }
7... Nc6
8. Nbd2 { The main line's position, reached in a different order. Everything learned there applies from here. } *
